{"id":412,"date":"2012-01-07T20:16:07","date_gmt":"2012-01-07T20:16:07","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/?page_id=412"},"modified":"2012-04-21T10:23:20","modified_gmt":"2012-04-21T10:23:20","slug":"useful-info","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/schools\/aveiro2012\/useful-info\/","title":{"rendered":"Useful Info"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>The event will be hosted at <a href=\"http:\/\/www.ieeta.pt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IEETA<\/a>, a modern building within the University of Aveiro campus. <\/p>\n<h1>Transportation<\/h1>\n<p>\nAveiro is located between two international airports (Porto is the nearest at 70 km and Lisbon at 260 km) and is connected to both airports by highway and railway networks. The highway network permits easy access to Aveiro by car from both Porto and Lisbon airports.<br \/>\nTravelling by train (visit train site) is the best option. Metro and Intercity\/Alfa Pendular trains have information in both Portuguese and English.<\/p>\n<h2>From Porto<\/h2>\n<h3>Train<\/h3>\n<p>\nYou can take a direct underground connection from Porto airport to the Campanh\u00e3 Railway Station (visit <a href=\"http:\/\/www.metrodoporto.pt\/en\/PageGen.aspx?SYS_PAGE_ID=\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Porto&#8217;s Underground site<\/a>). There you can choose between fast trains (Alfa Pendular, 30 min; Regular Intercity, 40 min) or slower trains (Urban or Regional trains, 50 min). For train time tables please visit <a href=\"http:\/\/www.cp.pt\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CP&#8217;s web page<\/a>. Please be aware of weekend schedules when searching for a train.<\/p>\n<h3>Taxi<\/h3>\n<p>\nFrom Porto a taxi ride will cost about \u20ac120. Please confirm the value with the taxi driver before leaving the airport.<\/p>\n<h3>Car Rental<\/h3>\n<p>\nPorto Airport has various car rental services. Please be aware of additional toll costs for the Porto-Aveiro journey.<\/p>\n<h2>From Lisbon<\/h2>\n<p>\nYou can take a taxi from airport to Oriente Railway Station (10 min; less than 10 euros) and then take the fast trains to Aveiro (Alfa Pendular, 2 hours; Regular Intercity trains, 2 hours 30 min). For train time tables please visit the trains web page. Please be aware of weekend schedules when searching for a train.<\/p>\n<h2>Aveiro<\/h2>\n<p>\nWhen you arrive at the Aveiro railway station the best option is to take a taxi directly to your hotel.<\/p>\n<hr>\n<h1>Accommodation<\/h1>\n<p>We are trying to find an official event hotel with discount prices. However, if you want to book your room now, there\u2019s a fine selection below.<\/p>\n<h3>Hotel Moliceiro<\/h3>\n<p>Hotel Moliceiro is priced at \u20ac67.5 per night single and \u20ac85 per night twin and includes buffet breakfast, welcome drink (Port wine and an &#8220;Ovo Mole&#8221;, the traditional Aveiro desert) and tea\/cookie service at dawn.<\/p>\n<h3>Hotel Meli\u00e1 Ria<\/h3>\n<p>Meli\u00e1 Ria is a top quality hotel located in the &#8220;Fonte Nova&#8221; zone in Aveiro with views over &#8220;Ria de Aveiro&#8221; and the Congress Centre. Meli\u00e1 Ria room pricing starts at \u20ac68 per night single without breakfast (additional \u20ac12).<br \/>\nMelia Ri\u00e1 is located at a 3 min taxi ride from Aveiro&#8217;s train station and is a 15 min walk from IEETA.<\/p>\n<h3>Hotel As Am\u00e9ricas<\/h3>\n<p>As Am\u00e9ricas Hotel offers a room with pricing of \u20ac65 per night single, including buffet breakfast.<br \/>\nAs Am\u00e9ricas hotel is a 5 min taxi ride from the train station and a 15 min walk from IEETA.<\/p>\n<h3>Residencial Jos\u00e9 Estev\u00e3o<\/h3>\n<p>Residencial Jos\u00e9 Estev\u00e3o offers rooms with prices starting at \u20ac45 per night single, including buffet breakfast.<br \/>\nResidencial Jos\u00e9 Estev\u00e3o is a 5 min taxi ride from the train station and a 5 min walk from IEETA.<\/p>\n<h3>Hotel das Salinas<\/h3>\n<p>Hotel das Salinas offer rooms with prices starting at \u20ac45 per night single, including buffet breakfast.<br \/>\nHotel das Salinas is a 10 min taxi ride from the train station and a 12 min walk from IEETA.<\/p>\n<hr>\n<h1>Other Information<\/h1>\n<h2>\nClimate and Clothing<br \/>\n<\/h2>\n<p>The weather in May is warm with temperatures around 18-22\u00b0 C during the day and 12-17\u00b0 C at night. It seldom rains and we advise you to bring light clothes and a swimming suit, just in case.<\/p>\n<h2>Local Currency<\/h2>\n<p>The Portuguese monetary unit is the EURO (\u20ac). Major credit cards are accepted in most shops and restaurants. There are several exchange offices and bank machines at the Porto and Lisbon airports, train stations and throughout Aveiro.<\/p>\n<h2>Electricity<\/h2>\n<p>Please bring electrical adaptors for any electrical appliances you bring. The electricity supply in Portugal is 220\/230V.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>The event will be hosted at IEETA, a modern building within the University of Aveiro campus. Transportation Aveiro is located between two international airports (Porto is the nearest at 70 km and Lisbon at 260 km) and is connected to &hellip; <a href=\"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/schools\/aveiro2012\/useful-info\/\">Continue reading <span class=\"meta-nav\">&rarr;<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"parent":351,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-412","page","type-page","status-publish","hentry"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/412","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=412"}],"